      <Patch Id="5hg3mMrPmSiNtJIrgCX9IT">
        <Canvas Id="LX9Qfslinueurn3KHUKDAr" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="0415Mxu07clrWuJoZCu179" Bounds="85,16,753,52" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="How To Blur an Image with a Control Mask">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">25</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="EDtznfq2pkYpns6VxnJITT" Bounds="85,85,520,94" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="2 x ShaderEffect [Qt] with blur_mask.frag&#xD;&#xA;- Mask: QtImage from LoadImage, black = sharp, white = blurred with Radius&#xD;&#xA;- Radius: blur radius in DIP where the mask is white&#xD;&#xA;- size: size of the picture in DIP (units x 100)&#xD;&#xA;- direction: (1, 0) pass 1 horizontal, (0, 1) pass 2 vertical">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="fapE9ZMaHA97FeR38SU6bM" Bounds="85,1279,839,262" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Blur an image by a different amount at every pixel, controlled by a grayscale mask. Grays in between blur proportionally. The mask is stretched over the picture.&#xD;&#xA;- Two passes: a Gaussian blur is separable. Pass 2 takes the result of pass 1. Both ShaderEffects run the same Fragment Code with the same radius, size and mask.&#xD;&#xA;- The shader always takes the same number of samples (the step between them grows with the radius), so the cost does not depend on the radius. size lets it turn the radius into texture coordinates.&#xD;&#xA;- Fragment Code is the text of shaders/blur_mask.frag next to this patch. One String pad feeds both passes; edit it live, errors show up at the Error pin of the ShaderEffect.&#xD;&#xA;- With a mask the blur is an approximation: the radius is read at the pixel that is drawn, in both passes. It is invisible for smooth masks, hard mask edges with a large radius can show a faint halo.&#xD;&#xA;- Radius 0 or a black mask returns the original pixel. Large radii are sampled coarsely, very fine detail then looks slightly stepped.&#xD;&#xA;- Every pass is a separate layer. Changing Radius or the mask re-renders both passes, the picture itself is rendered once.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="DMRYQcvp25z6TyOBdQ4wBP" Bounds="203,240,845,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="1  Two QtImages: the picture and the mask (black = sharp, white = Radius). The mask only drives the blur, it is not drawn.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
